* TWO-LEVEL MEMO DATABASE -- A PROBE, NOT A SPEC. 2026-08-30.
*
* THE OWNER'S QUESTION, VERBATIM: "have we tested putting a database A in a
* memo field and then move the containing Database B into database C?"
*
* THE ANSWER BEFORE RUNNING ANYTHING: one level ships and is proven
* (workspace_minidb.dts, DB_T3/DB_T4; 30 of 37 MINIDB containers carry a nested
* .dtx). TWO levels are NOT BLOCKED -- they are UNGUARDED, which is a different
* problem and the reason this probe exists rather than a bug report.
*
* MEASURED IN SOURCE 2026-08-30, and this is what the probe is checking against:
*
*   DEPTH        cmd_workspace.cpp:3358 and :3690 -- TWO writers, BOTH write the
*                literal "0". No hydration path ever writes it. A column whose
*                own declaration calls it the "MANDATORY recursion declaration"
*                answers the same for a leaf and for something nested five deep.
*   PAYLOAD_SHA  NO WRITER AT ALL. Chartered as "integrity + cycle-detection
*                material", so the cycle detector has no material.
*   EST_HYD_B    the sum of the container's FILE lengths -- a nested container's
*                SERIALIZED bytes, not its HYDRATED expansion. Admission control
*                asks the wrong number at every level below the first.
*   SELF_REF     posture.find("WORKSPACES") != npos. A substring test on posture
*                text, wrong in both directions: a table named
*                WORKSPACES_ARCHIVE flags T, an embedded catalog under another
*                name flags F.
*
* PREDICTIONS, WRITTEN BEFORE THE RUN so a miss is visible rather than absorbed:
*
*   P1  level-1 save succeeds; FMT "MINIDB 1", DEPTH 0, SELF_REF F, SIZE_B > 0.
*   P2  level-2 save SUCCEEDS -- the container format is length-prefixed and
*       binary-safe, so a FILE section carries the catalog's .dtx whole.
*   P3  level-2 DEPTH reads 0. THAT IS THE DEFECT: it is the number that should
*       read 1, and nothing anywhere can produce a 1.
*   P4  level-2 SELF_REF reads T -- correctly, but BY ACCIDENT, because the
*       posture names WORKSPACES as a table rather than because anything
*       inspected the payload.
*   P5  hydrating the OUTER container lands a WORKSPACES table in RAM whose
*       memo still carries the INNER container, so twl_inner is still a row.
*       Two levels round-trip, uncounted and unguarded.
*
* IF P2 OR P5 FAIL the answer is better news than the predictions: the format
* refuses what nothing declares, and the guard columns are describing a case
* that cannot arise. Read a failure that way rather than as a defect.
*
* RESULTS, 2026-08-30, run against c773f8b7. ALL FIVE PREDICTIONS HELD.
*
*   twl_inner   MINIDB 1  DEPTH 0  SELF_REF F  SIZE_B  4763  EST_HYD_B  4438
*   twl_outer   MINIDB 1  DEPTH 0  SELF_REF T  SIZE_B 28859  EST_HYD_B 28480
*   P5          twl_inner is a readable row inside the hydrated outer catalog
*
* AND FOUR THINGS THE PREDICTIONS DID NOT REACH:
*
* COMPOUNDING. The transcript was run TWO -- row numbers gave it away and the
* directory confirmed it. Run 1 produced outer 11,276 B; run 2 produced 28,859,
* because the outer now carries a catalog holding run 1's inner AND outer. Each
* save of the containing database swallows every container already in it. The
* scratch catalog is 4,079 B of table against a 54,032 B sidecar.
*
* THE SIDECAR LANDS ON REAL DISK AND THE ARITHMETIC CLOSES EXACTLY.
* data/ram/WORKSPACES.dtx, 25,104 B, timestamped at the run, SURVIVING the
* unmount. VFS 3,376 + disk 25,104 = 28,480 = EST_HYD_B, to the byte. So
* EST_HYD_B is exact as a TOTAL and wrong as what it is chartered to be, a RAM
* budget input -- the non-sidecar subtotal it should carry is computed nowhere.
*
* TWO SHIPPED MESSAGES ARE FALSE FOR MEMO CONTENT. "zero disk reads" counts
* disk bytes as RAM bytes; "all RAM files dropped" is true of the VFS and
* structurally incapable of covering a real file. Seven stale sidecars under the
* RAM root, 68 KB, oldest 2026-08-12 -- and NOTHING anywhere removes them.
*
* P5 IS WEAKER THAN IT LOOKS, SAID PLAINLY. It proves the inner ROW round-trips
* (WS_NAME/FMT/DEPTH/SIZE_B all live in the .dbf). The inner PAYLOAD is proven
* only indirectly, by the 25,104-byte sidecar on disk. The decisive arm nobody
* has run is WORKSPACE LOAD twl_inner MEMO RAM from INSIDE the hydrated catalog.
* It also tripped the blind-USE shape: "already open in current area 0", because
* LOAD had opened it -- correct here by luck, since that cursor is the RAM file.
*
* RUN 3, 2026-08-30, AGAINST THE REPAIRED BUILD (72318f58) -- AND IT FALSIFIED
* THIS PROBE'S OWN PREDICTION FOR THE REASON THIS PROBE EXISTS TO REPORT.
* The repair was predicted to print "3376 B into the RAM disk, 25104 B of memo
* sidecar(s) onto REAL DISK". It printed 4782 and 58864. The STRUCTURE was
* right and the NUMBERS were run 2's: the probe is not self-cleaning, so run 3
* carries run 2's containers and the outer grew 28,859 -> 64,025 B. COMPOUNDING
* INVALIDATED THE PREDICTION ABOUT COMPOUNDING. Growth by generation: 2.56x
* then 2.22x.
*
* THE SPLIT IS EXACT, AND AN INDEPENDENT COUNTER AGREES.
*     4,782 + 58,864 = 63,646  = the reported total and EST_HYD_B
*     VDISK RAM bytes = 4,782  -- the VFS counted separately, to the byte
*     data/ram/WORKSPACES.dtx  = 58,864 B on disk, likewise
* Two counters that could disagree and do not. "zero disk reads" is gone; the
* line now names where each half of the payload went.
*
* AND THE OLD DEFECT GOT WORSE EVERY GENERATION, which is the argument for
* having fixed it rather than documented it: admission would have claimed
* 63,646 B of RAM budget for 4,782 B actually resident -- 13.3x, up from 8.4x
* one run earlier. 92% of this payload is not RAM-resident.
*
* Findings recorded in AIF-120 (grandfathered, R133), not given a number.
*
* SELF-ISOLATING. The WORKSPACES slot is re-pointed at a scratch root before
* anything is written, the r131_durable_root_probe precedent, so the production
* catalog is never opened. Run it with an ABSOLUTE path:
*   DOTSCRIPT D:\code\ccode\dottalkpp\data\scripts\two_level_memo_probe.dts
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH WORKSPACES tmp/ws2lvl
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE TWLA CONFIRM
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-PROBE-BEGIN"
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LEVEL 1 -- a table with a live memo field, saved into the catalog's memo.
SELECT 0
CREATE X64 TWLA (ID N(4,0), NOTES M)
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE NOTES WITH "level one payload"
? "TWL_G0_inner_memo_written:" + (NOTES = "level one payload")
WORKSPACE SAVE twl_inner MEMO MINIDB
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
* P1 -- what the catalog says about a LEAF container.
SET PATH DBF tmp/ws2lvl
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P1-BEGIN"
SELECT 0
USE WORKSPACES
SMARTLIST WS_NAME,FMT,DEPTH,SELF_REF,SIZE_B,EST_HYD_B FOR ALLTRIM(WS_NAME) = "twl_inner"
CLOSE
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P1-END"
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LEVEL 2 -- put the CONTAINING database into a container. The catalog itself
* is the table this posture opens, so its .dtx -- which is where level one now
* lives -- rides along as a FILE section.
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P2-BEGIN"
SELECT 0
USE WORKSPACES
WORKSPACE SAVE twl_outer MEMO MINIDB
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P2-END"
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
* P3/P4 -- the two guard columns on the NESTED row.
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P3-BEGIN"
SELECT 0
USE WORKSPACES
SMARTLIST WS_NAME,FMT,DEPTH,SELF_REF,SIZE_B,EST_HYD_B FOR ALLTRIM(WS_NAME) = "twl_outer"
CLOSE
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P3-END"
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* P5 -- THE ROUND TRIP, AND THE ONE THAT ANSWERS THE QUESTION. Hydrate the
* OUTER container into RAM and look for the INNER row inside the catalog it
* carried. If twl_inner is listed, two levels survived a save and a load with
* nothing counting them.
DO mem
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P5-BEGIN"
WORKSPACE LOAD twl_outer MEMO RAM
VDISK STATUS
SELECT 0
USE WORKSPACES
SMARTLIST WS_NAME,FMT,DEPTH,SIZE_B FOR ALLTRIM(WS_NAME) = "twl_inner"
CLOSE
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-P5-END"
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
VDISK UNMOUNT
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TEARDOWN. The scratch catalog root is left in place deliberately -- it is
* under the gitignored TMP slot and it is the evidence.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
ERASE TWLA CONFIRM
SET PATH WORKSPACES workspaces
FORMULA "TWOLEVEL-PROBE-END"
DO x64
